AUTOTOP: MUSB host (U DISK): back to mainline 4.19 in the two places the
vendor changed under NICHOLAS_ADD and downstream linux-arkmicro c195cb9
reverted: TX FIFO flush retries (vendor 1, mainline 1000: gives up at once
under load) and forcing transfers of 64 bytes or less onto PIO. Goes with
the Inventra DMA the spike config now enables; stock moves U DISK data with
the controller's own DMA (one DMA interrupt per 512-byte packet, 19 MB/s),
while the PIO-only 4.19 spike reset the stick mid-read under load (SPIKE16).
